WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

01:53.860 --> 01:59.030
<b>The urban legends floating around about the
warm-colored and cold-colored balls of light.</b>

01:59.030 --> 02:03.330
<b>The beings you can yet can’t see that the
children are spreading rumors about.</b>

02:03.330 --> 02:05.170
<b>This winter is strange.</b>

02:05.170 --> 02:07.000
<b>It’s the same as the summer
of two years ago.</b>

02:09.910 --> 02:11.410
<b>Once the conditions are met...</b>

02:11.410 --> 02:15.380
<b>...what happened on the night of the
Cat Dance may very well repeat itself.</b>

02:37.160 --> 02:44.150
<b>A Problem We Can’</b>t Participate In

03:11.730 --> 03:12.500
<b>Hey.</b>

03:13.640 --> 03:14.800
<b>Hi.</b>

03:14.800 --> 03:16.340
<b>Got a minute?</b>

03:19.810 --> 03:22.010
<b>I just feel like talking.</b>

03:23.210 --> 03:24.480
<b>About Bun-chan?</b>

03:25.550 --> 03:27.380
<b>Can’t I talk about myself around you?</b>

03:28.950 --> 03:35.460
<b>I forget. Did I tell you I was in the
3-dan league at the Shoreikai?</b>

03:35.460 --> 03:36.820
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:36.830 --> 03:39.660
<b>You said you needed to become 4-dan or something.</b>

03:39.660 --> 03:40.860
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:40.860 --> 03:44.300
<b>After half a year of fighting in the 3-dan league...</b>

03:44.300 --> 03:48.240
<b>...the two people with the most wins can go pro.</b>

03:48.240 --> 03:51.510
<b>In other words, only four people
can go pro in a single year.</b>

03:52.340 --> 03:53.970
<b>That sure is tight...</b>

03:54.640 --> 03:56.280
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:56.280 --> 03:59.050
<b>You have to climb this huge
wall before becoming a pro.</b>

03:59.050 --> 04:01.450
<b>The wall to the 4-dan rank.</b>

04:01.450 --> 04:05.390
<b>If someone isn’t able to cross the
wall before he turns twenty-six...</b>

04:05.390 --> 04:07.690
<b>...he can no longer become a pro.</b>

04:07.690 --> 04:09.720
<b>That means you still have a little
less than ten years left.</b>

04:10.490 --> 04:12.460
<b>I only have ten years left...</b>

04:13.660 --> 04:16.830
<b>There have been hundreds of
promising shogi players...</b>

04:16.830 --> 04:20.940
<b>...who’ve given up on going pro since they
were unable to defeat that wall.</b>

04:20.940 --> 04:25.070
<b>And starting next year, even more young
players will start climbing at an alarming rate.</b>

04:35.450 --> 04:37.490
<b>What is it?</b>

04:37.490 --> 04:39.820
<b>It looks like... you’ve changed a little.</b>

04:41.490 --> 04:44.060
<b>You smile a lot more now
than you used to.</b>

04:46.230 --> 04:48.460
<b>When’s your next match?</b>

04:48.460 --> 04:49.200
<b>Tomorrow.</b>

04:51.770 --> 04:52.670
<b>It’s really amazing...</b>

04:53.300 --> 04:55.240
<b>What is?</b>

04:55.240 --> 04:57.040
<b>Where you’re at.</b>

04:57.040 --> 05:00.640
<b>But to me, it’s just normal.</b>

05:01.140 --> 05:03.340
<b>Normal, huh?</b>

05:03.350 --> 05:05.650
<b>I wonder what “normal” is...</b>

05:08.580 --> 05:10.850
<b>If I really have changed...</b>

05:11.350 --> 05:13.950
<b>...it’s because of Bun-chan.</b>

05:13.960 --> 05:15.720
<b>Yeah.</b>

05:15.720 --> 05:18.660
<b>For someone like me
who can’t do anything...</b>

05:18.660 --> 05:21.660
<b>...everything would probably stay
the same if I weren’t here.</b>

05:21.660 --> 05:23.400
<b>You’re wrong.</b>

05:25.100 --> 05:27.100
<b>It would bother me if you weren’t here.</b>

05:30.840 --> 05:33.570
<b>If you weren’t here
at times like these, Kisa...</b>

05:33.580 --> 05:35.780
<b>...I just wouldn’t know who to talk with.</b>

05:37.950 --> 05:39.850
<b>It’s the truth!</b>

05:41.320 --> 05:42.320
<b>Umm...</b>

05:43.490 --> 05:44.850
<b>You know...</b>

05:47.260 --> 05:48.560
<b>How should I put this...</b>

05:58.800 --> 06:00.540
<b>Out of Area</b>

06:00.540 --> 06:03.670
<b>Where could Sukawara-san be?</b>

06:04.510 --> 06:09.940
<b>I’m positive that this has something
to do with the material fairies, too...</b>

06:10.680 --> 06:14.980
<b>Attention. The ferris wheel will be closing for today.</b>

06:14.980 --> 06:19.420
<b>Please follow the officials’ instructions,
and leave the area.</b>

06:19.420 --> 06:21.360
<b>Out of Area</b>

06:23.690 --> 06:26.990
<b>I never thought
I’d get stranded in the city...</b>

06:30.930 --> 06:33.000
<b>And I’m supposed to be the one
who <i>reports</i> the news...</b>

06:33.000 --> 06:35.670
<b>...not the one who gets reported on.</b>

06:44.080 --> 06:46.180
<b>Geez.</b>

