<b>Riezo</b>

07:14.080 --> 07:15.910
<b>Hey, you.</b>

07:15.910 --> 07:19.850
<b>The one obsessed with taking
pictures on his cellphone.</b>

07:23.550 --> 07:24.550
<b>Me?</b>

07:24.550 --> 07:28.320
<b>You’re the boy who was talking to
Sukawara Akira the other day, right?</b>

07:29.990 --> 07:34.800
<b>Hey... could you tell me if she’s in Yokohama
because of the material fairies?</b>

07:36.470 --> 07:37.430
<b>What are you talking about?</b>

07:40.340 --> 07:41.900
<b>You don’t have to hide it from me.</b>

07:41.900 --> 07:45.970
<b>And after that reaction,
you must have seen something.</b>

07:45.970 --> 07:48.410
<b>I’ve also seen them.</b>

07:48.410 --> 07:51.350
<b>Do you know about the book
“The Summer of the Fairies”?</b>

07:52.610 --> 07:54.550
<b>Yeah, I’ve read it...</b>

07:54.550 --> 07:57.890
<b>I was at the place
where that event happened.</b>

07:58.790 --> 08:01.320
<b>You mean the night of the
Cat Dance the book was about?</b>

08:01.320 --> 08:04.030
<b>That’s right. That’s why I’m somewhat
interested in them.</b>

08:04.030 --> 08:08.000
<b>So, could you tell me what you
and Sukawara talked about?</b>

08:15.140 --> 08:16.700
<b>So what did you want to talk about?</b>

08:16.710 --> 08:20.240
<b>Don’t you think things will be bad
for Kisa at the rate they’re going?</b>

08:20.240 --> 08:21.940
<b>What do you mean by “bad”?</b>

08:21.940 --> 08:23.940
<b>I met with her earlier,
and she seemed fine.</b>

08:26.820 --> 08:29.920
<b>At the rate things are going, Kisa...</b>

08:29.920 --> 08:33.950
<b>...won’t be able to go on to the
next grade, the teacher said.</b>

08:33.960 --> 08:35.460
<b>So that’s what you’re talking about, huh?</b>

08:35.460 --> 08:40.290
<b>Could you tell her to show her
face at school once in a while?</b>

08:40.300 --> 08:41.430
<b>Why me?</b>

08:41.430 --> 08:45.770
<b>Because... it seems you’ve been
seeing her a lot recently.</b>

08:45.770 --> 08:48.040
<b>And if I push too hard...</b>

08:48.040 --> 08:50.710
<b>...she’ll probably think I’m a
teacher’s pet or something.</b>

08:50.710 --> 08:53.240
<b>Well you <i>are</i> the class representative type.</b>

08:53.240 --> 08:55.280
<b>Don’t make fun of me.</b>

08:56.980 --> 08:59.310
<b>I understand a lot’s going on with her right now, but...</b>

08:59.310 --> 09:03.250
<b>...if Kisa doesn’t actively change by herself,
I don’t think anything will be resolved.</b>

09:03.250 --> 09:06.790
<b>If she doesn’t pull herself together...</b>

09:06.790 --> 09:10.730
<b>People always say the same
things to those being bullied.</b>

09:10.730 --> 09:13.690
<b>“The problem lies with the person being bullied.”</b>

09:15.100 --> 09:17.770
<b>How is she supposed to change?</b>

09:17.770 --> 09:19.800
<b>If she just acts the same
as everyone else...</b>

09:19.800 --> 09:21.700
<b>...will she really be able to change?</b>

09:21.700 --> 09:24.270
<b>She’ll still hate the people who
forced her out of school.</b>

09:24.270 --> 09:28.680
<b>Those individuals who can’t fit in with
the group tend to feel alienated.</b>

09:29.580 --> 09:31.810
<b>I’m the same as Kisa.</b>

09:31.810 --> 09:33.280
<b>I was the same.</b>

09:33.280 --> 09:35.450
<b>I was “Crybaby Shigeki.”</b>

09:35.450 --> 09:36.780
<b>But...</b>

09:36.790 --> 09:38.690
<b>Kisa may have been avoiding
going to school...</b>

09:38.690 --> 09:42.960
<b>...but I’m sure she still wants
to be a part of it.</b>

09:42.960 --> 09:45.730
<b>That’s why she’s just avoiding
going to class.</b>

09:45.730 --> 09:48.200
<b>If she didn’t want to be a part of it,
she would’ve dropped out already.</b>

09:48.200 --> 09:50.870
<b>But you and Kisa are different.</b>

09:50.870 --> 09:53.100
<b>You have your shogi, but...</b>

09:53.100 --> 09:55.070
<b>...right now, Kisa has nothing.</b>

09:55.070 --> 09:57.410
<b>She has nothing?</b>

09:57.410 --> 09:59.470
<b>Why do you decide things like that all on your own?</b>

10:01.680 --> 10:03.710
<b>You say you want to help her out...</b>

10:03.710 --> 10:05.580
<b>You say you want to support her.</b>

10:05.580 --> 10:09.050
<b>But aren’t you just saying that to satisfy yourself?</b>

10:10.050 --> 10:11.520
<b>There’s no reason to take that tone...</b>

10:11.520 --> 10:15.090
<b>I’m... worried about Kisa.</b>

10:15.090 --> 10:17.220
<b>Even our teacher worries.</b>

10:17.230 --> 10:19.060
<b>I don’t really want to say this, but...</b>

10:19.060 --> 10:23.160
<b>...Kisa’s parents have basically abandoned her.</b>

10:23.170 --> 10:25.530
<b>That’s why I...</b>

10:26.100 --> 10:29.040
<b>What do you know about Kisa?</b>

10:29.040 --> 10:32.810
<b>And what can you possibly know about my shogi?</b>

10:50.300 --> 10:52.870
<b>Tokimiya</b>

10:58.900 --> 11:01.040
<b>If you have some business here,
just say so.</b>

11:01.040 --> 11:05.440
<b>Go home if you don’t,
because standing there is unsettling.</b>

11:07.340 --> 11:09.610
<b>Umm... well...</b>

11:09.610 --> 11:12.280
<b>If it’s about Rieko,
I already sent her home.</b>

11:12.280 --> 11:14.420
<b>No... I was wondering if Sukawara-san...</b>

11:14.420 --> 11:16.320
<b>She hasn’t returned yet.</b>

11:17.590 --> 11:20.050
<b>Never mind, then...</b>

11:26.930 --> 11:27.030
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.030 --> 11:27.100
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.100 --> 11:27.200
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.200 --> 11:27.330
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.330 --> 11:27.430
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.430 --> 11:27.570
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.570 --> 11:27.700
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.700 --> 11:27.830
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.700 --> 11:30.230
<b>It’s already been seven hours, huh...?</b>

11:27.830 --> 11:27.930
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:27.930 --> 11:30.230
<b>Out of Area</b>

11:33.570 --> 11:37.540
<b>“It’s cold, so let’s warm
each other up,” is it?</b>

11:38.070 --> 11:42.010
<b>A lot must be going on
in these gondolas...</b>

11:51.420 --> 11:53.750
<b>I heard you got into a fight with Rieko.</b>

11:53.760 --> 11:55.620
<b>I said a little too much...</b>

11:56.290 --> 11:58.090
<b>And because you’re stuck on that...</b>

11:58.090 --> 12:00.960
<b>...you can’t focus on tomorrow’s match?</b>

12:00.960 --> 12:02.960
<b>There’s that too, but...</b>

12:04.470 --> 12:07.870
<b>It’s been a while,
so do you want to play?</b>

12:10.310 --> 12:11.570
<b>Please.</b>

12:21.620 --> 12:23.920
<b>Tokimiya</b>

12:27.690 --> 12:29.060
<b>Please.</b>

12:35.000 --> 12:38.430
<b>Is Kisa not going to school?</b>

12:38.430 --> 12:41.200
<b>There are nights when she doesn’t even return home.</b>

12:41.200 --> 12:44.440
<b>But she does return in the end,
doesn’t she?</b>

12:44.440 --> 12:46.970
<b>I call it “mini-running away.”</b>

12:46.980 --> 12:49.810
<b>“Mini-running away,” huh?</b>

12:49.810 --> 12:54.080
<b>By pretending it’s a fad or something,
you obscure the real problem.</b>

12:55.980 --> 12:58.590
<b>I wonder if she’s scared of looking straight at them.</b>

12:58.590 --> 12:59.550
<b>Looking at who?</b>

13:00.120 --> 13:01.490
<b>The company she’s keeping.</b>

13:01.490 --> 13:03.220
<b>You should understand.</b>

13:04.390 --> 13:07.560
<b>Because you’re playing one
big game of hide-and-seek.</b>

13:07.560 --> 13:11.030
<b>One seeking, the other hiding.</b>

13:11.030 --> 13:15.340
<b>The seeker is looking for the other, alone.</b>

13:15.340 --> 13:21.480
<b>The hider fears being found.</b>

13:21.480 --> 13:23.340
<b>Both are full of helpless anxiety.</b>

13:26.180 --> 13:31.250
<b>Yet you continue living out your lives,
seeking and being found forever.</b>

13:33.560 --> 13:34.220
<b>I...</b>

13:34.220 --> 13:39.690
<b>You came here tonight seeking
out yourself, didn’t you?</b>

13:42.430 --> 13:45.400
<b>[Yamato Real Estate]</b>

13:48.940 --> 13:50.140
<b>Why did I say those things...?</b>

13:52.340 --> 13:56.440
<b>Since Kisa’s birthday is coming up,
I was thinking of throwing her a party...</b>

13:56.450 --> 13:59.050
<b>I wanted to talk about that, but...</b>

13:59.050 --> 14:03.550
<b>...I talked to Shigeki about school instead...</b>

14:07.420 --> 14:11.490
<b>I’m always playing the good, obedient girl in
front of the teachers and my parents, but...</b>

14:12.360 --> 14:13.960
<b>I’m really the worst.</b>

14:17.300 --> 14:18.630
<b>Don’t need this...</b>

14:19.500 --> 14:20.900
<b>Don’t need this...</b>

14:20.900 --> 14:23.000
<b>Save.</b>

14:23.000 --> 14:24.000
<b>Don’t need this...</b>

14:24.010 --> 14:26.010
<b><i>Really</i> don’t need this one!</b>

14:26.010 --> 14:27.680
<b>Save.</b>

14:31.510 --> 14:32.950
<b>Don’t need this...</b>

14:38.820 --> 14:42.160
<b>Even now, I’m chasing my dream as a journalist.</b>

14:42.160 --> 14:43.820
<b>Just like I was back then.</b>

14:43.830 --> 14:49.030
<b>But... I didn’t really mean to ignore you back then...</b>

14:49.800 --> 14:51.530
<b>All I wanted...</b>

14:53.270 --> 14:57.870
<b>...was a partner who could understand
my work, wasn’t it?</b>

15:11.190 --> 15:13.490
<b>Tomorrow’s the 3-dan league match, right?</b>

15:13.490 --> 15:15.520
<b>Should you be staying up late like this?</b>

15:16.530 --> 15:19.560
<b>I wouldn’t be able to sleep anyway,
the way I am now.</b>

15:19.560 --> 15:21.930
<b>I think this’ll be
the 9th match now, right?</b>

15:21.930 --> 15:25.230
<b>The people who have lost twice
fight each other in this match.</b>

15:25.230 --> 15:28.040
<b>Winning or losing in this match
will be critical.</b>

15:28.040 --> 15:29.000
<b>And my opponent is...</b>

15:31.210 --> 15:34.880
<b>...really popular, and is expected
to be an expert in the future.</b>

15:34.880 --> 15:36.840
<b>A genius.</b>

15:36.850 --> 15:39.480
<b>Over the past two years in the Shoreikai...</b>

15:39.480 --> 15:41.220
<b>...I haven’t won a match against him once.</b>

15:41.220 --> 15:42.980
<b>That’s great.</b>

15:44.150 --> 15:48.420
<b>The people who are more skilled
than you will make you better.</b>

15:48.990 --> 15:53.060
<b>When someone faces a great
opponent, he will advance.</b>

15:53.060 --> 15:55.860
<b>If he’s able to face the opponent properly, that is.</b>

15:55.860 --> 15:56.730
<b>But...</b>

15:56.730 --> 15:58.300
<b>The opponent’s too great this time?</b>

15:59.940 --> 16:02.940
<b>You’ve already lost if that’s what you’re thinking.</b>

16:02.940 --> 16:05.540
<b>Your feelings have already fled from you.</b>

16:05.540 --> 16:07.270
<b>But what am I supposed to...</b>

16:07.280 --> 16:13.580
<b>There’s nothing you can do but
play your own shogi, right?</b>

16:13.580 --> 16:16.520
<b>It’s fine if you just collide with him,
believing in your own shogi.</b>

16:17.290 --> 16:20.490
<b>That’s what it means to properly face your opponent.</b>

16:25.490 --> 16:27.160
<b>I lose.</b>

16:28.100 --> 16:30.160
<b>You’ve certainly become strong, huh?</b>

16:30.170 --> 16:32.670
<b>I’m strong enough to teach people,
but I can’t beat you.</b>

16:33.600 --> 16:38.140
<b>Though I’m the one who taught
you how to move these pieces.</b>

16:38.140 --> 16:42.510
<b>I’m sorry... I don’t remember that.</b>

16:42.510 --> 16:45.710
<b>As you age, you only tend to remember
some specific things, huh?</b>

16:45.710 --> 16:48.150
<b>For example, with me, it might be... your name.</b>

16:49.620 --> 16:55.590
<b>Shigeki</b>

16:50.090 --> 16:54.160
<b>Written as “moto wo nasu,”
your name means “make base.”</b>

16:54.160 --> 16:55.590
<b>Your name originated from “Macbeth.”</b>

16:56.430 --> 16:58.660
<b>Shakespeare?</b>

16:58.660 --> 17:02.100
<b>When your father was still a dreaming
youngster whose mind was filled with plays...</b>

17:02.100 --> 17:05.070
<b>...he often came here to eat.</b>

17:05.070 --> 17:07.070
<b>But my dad’s a...</b>

17:07.070 --> 17:09.380
<b>A stubborn policeman?</b>

17:10.410 --> 17:14.340
<b>What your eyes see isn’t all that’s
out there, in every sense.</b>

17:17.780 --> 17:19.350
<b>What’s your problem?!</b>

17:20.580 --> 17:21.950
<b>I can’t believe you!</b>

17:21.950 --> 17:24.820
<b>It’s impossible to stay with you! Let’s break up!</b>

17:27.290 --> 17:28.720
<b>W-Wait!</b>

17:30.290 --> 17:32.190
<b>No one knows what the future holds...</b>

17:40.700 --> 17:44.210
<b>How was it to be trapped
in that small space...</b>

17:44.210 --> 17:47.610
<b>...isolated in mid-air before finally
being released nine hours later?</b>

17:49.210 --> 17:50.780
<b>How do you feel right now?</b>

17:55.220 --> 17:57.020
<b>Trouble with your cell phones...</b>

17:57.020 --> 17:58.690
<b>Traffic light malfunctions...</b>

17:58.690 --> 18:00.320
<b>Bugs in security systems...</b>

18:00.320 --> 18:03.190
<b>All the way to mayhem with
your computer networks...</b>

18:03.190 --> 18:08.130
<b>In Yokohama, there have been various and
repeated occurrences of such problems.</b>

18:08.130 --> 18:11.700
<b>We can see that these cases have
all involved electronics...</b>

18:11.700 --> 18:14.600
<b>...and people have claimed that this might
be some sort of cyberterrorism...</b>

18:14.600 --> 18:16.940
<b>...but even after some thorough investigation...</b>

18:16.940 --> 18:19.470
<b>...the true origin of these issues
has yet to be determined.</b>

18:20.040 --> 18:21.310
<b>And on the other hand...</b>

18:21.310 --> 18:26.480
<b>...why have the children been spreading
so many urban legends recently?</b>

18:27.020 --> 18:29.250
<b>Am I alone in thinking that today’s event...</b>

18:29.250 --> 18:34.460
<b>...is not completely unrelated to everything
that’s been going on?</b>

18:35.560 --> 18:36.420
<b>Here you are.</b>

18:36.430 --> 18:37.760
<b>Thank you...</b>

18:41.760 --> 18:42.830
<b>Who was that woman?</b>

